# Web app environment variables
#
# ===========================================================================
#  PRODUCTION CHECKLIST — the three URLs below MUST be changed off localhost
#  before you deploy, or the live site silently breaks:
#    * NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL  -> /chat, provider grid, usage all go offline
#    * WORKER_VALIDATE_URL      -> API-key validation requests fail
#    * NEXT_PUBLIC_RELAY_URL    -> login / dashboard auth fails
#  Each is spelled out in the comment directly above it.
# ===========================================================================

# >>> PRODUCTION-CRITICAL <<<
# Base URL of the Zintus gateway the web app talks to for chat, provider status,
# and usage/savings (lib/gateway.ts). Defaults to http://localhost:8788 for local
# dev.
#
# NOTE: Zintus is local-first / BYOK. There is NO hosted gateway — each user
# runs their own with `zintus serve`, so a public deploy of this site is just a
# thin client. If you ship a default/shared deploy, leave this pointed at the
# user's own gateway (localhost) and the /chat offline state will guide them to
# `zintus serve`. Only override it when you actually operate a reachable gateway
# (e.g. https://gateway.yourdomain.com).
#
# WHAT BREAKS IF WRONG: if a deployed (non-localhost) site keeps the localhost
# default, every visitor's browser tries http://localhost:8788 on THEIR machine
# — chat, the provider grid, and the usage UI all render as "no gateway
# connected" / unavailable.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:8788

# NOTE: there is intentionally NO NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_TOKEN. The web app talks to
# the gateway from the browser, and any NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the
# public client JS bundle — a bearer token set here would be exposed to every
# visitor. The hosted web therefore targets a token-less LOOPBACK gateway. If you
# expose a gateway on a network and need auth, front it with a server-side proxy
# or session cookie; do not ship a static token in this client bundle.

# >>> PRODUCTION-CRITICAL <<<
# Cloudflare validate-key worker URL used by the key-validation proxy
# (lib/worker.ts). When neither WORKER_VALIDATE_URL nor VALIDATE_WORKER_URL is
# set, it falls back to http://127.0.0.1:8787/validate — fine for local dev, but
# in production (e.g. Vercel) that localhost default is unreachable, so API-key
# validation requests fail (users can't verify keys). Set this (or the
# VALIDATE_WORKER_URL alias) to the deployed worker URL in production.
# WORKER_VALIDATE_URL takes precedence.
WORKER_VALIDATE_URL=https://your-worker.workers.dev/validate

# Alternate env name also supported (used only if WORKER_VALIDATE_URL is unset)
# VALIDATE_WORKER_URL=

# Canonical production origin for SEO metadata routes (app/robots.ts,
# app/sitemap.ts) and absolute URLs. Defaults to https://www.zintus.ai; override
# for preview/staging deployments so robots.txt and sitemap.xml emit the right host.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.zintus.ai

# Optional server-side quota ledger path
# ZINTUS_QUOTA_PATH=/tmp/zintus-quota.db

# --- Zintus Cloud dashboard -----------------------------------------------
# >>> PRODUCTION-CRITICAL <<<
# URL of the relay Cloudflare Worker. The dashboard pages (/login, /dashboard)
# call this API for auth and session management. If left unset/localhost in
# production, login and the dashboard fail to authenticate.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RELAY_URL=https://relay.zintus.ai

# --- Hosted Judge Live Mode ------------------------------------------------
# Leave disabled for ordinary public web deployments. When enabled, /judge
# exchanges an invitation code for a short-lived HttpOnly cookie, then proxies a
# tightly allowlisted Engineer session to a private gateway. These values are
# SERVER-ONLY: never prefix them with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# The gateway must be HTTPS, private to this deployment, configured for exactly
# the fixture repository below, and must itself enforce a global spend limit.
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_DEMO_ENABLED=1
# Set this instead of the invitation-code setting when the time-boxed
# Engineering Premium experience should open directly. It applies only to the
# Engineer BFF route; it does not enable managed keys for Chat or other Zintus features.
# ZINTUS_ENGINEER_PREMIUM_ENABLED=1
# Optional absolute expiry for a time-boxed Premium Engineering window.
# ZINTUS_ENGINEER_PREMIUM_EXPIRES_AT=2026-08-21T23:59:59Z
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GATEWAY_URL=/api/judge/gateway
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_GATEWAY_URL=https://engineer-gateway.example.com
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=server-only-gateway-bearer-token
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_SESSION_SECRET=at-least-32-random-characters
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_ACCESS_CODE_HASH=<sha256 hex of the invitation code; omit when Premium is enabled>
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_FIXTURE_REPOSITORY_ID=judge-repository
#
# Hard ceilings applied server-side to every new judge run. Any one of these
# limits pauses execution; the $10 ceiling remains the spending authority.
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_RUN_COST_USD=10
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_RUN_TOKEN_BUDGET=700000
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_RUN_TIME_SECONDS=1500
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=1200
# ZINTUS_JUDGE_MAX_REQUEST_CHARS=6000
